CommonError.description:
A common error data type used in a business error, contains a string `code` type and `msg`.

 It's always used as the default error data type in responses, e.g:

 ```json
 {
     "ok": false,
     "data": {
         "code": "permission_denied",
         "msg": "You don't have permission to access this resource"
     }
 }
 ```

is_hidden.description:
Hidden by the platform. Only its uploader gets it from the detail endpoints; lists leave
 it out.
 @since 261008
